{
	"format_version": "1.21.6",
	"credit": "Inventory icon of the advanced cannon mount, assembled verbatim from the three authored world models: block/advanced_cannon_mount/advanced_cannon_mount.json (base plinth), block/advanced_cannon_mount/fire_control_rotating.json (turntable cradle, raised rails) and block/advanced_cannon_mount/carriage_axle.json (brass drive axle). No geometry or UV was re-authored - every element and face UV is copied from those files, so the icon samples the same art the block uses (cbc_firecontrol:block/advanced_cannon_mount for the plinth, :block/fire_control_rotating for the cradle, :block/brass_axis / :block/brass_axis_top for the axle). Cradle and axle get +8 Y because the world renderer translates them 0.5 block (BERenderer/Visual); the earlier icon used create:block/brass_block, a generic brass panel, which is why the inventory render did not look like the mount. The display block is the transform list of minecraft:block/block multiplied by 0.8 (gui 0.625 -> 0.5, ground 0.25 -> 0.2, fixed 0.5 -> 0.4, thirdperson_righthand 0.375 -> 0.3, firstperson 0.40 -> 0.32), read from assets/minecraft/models/block/block.json in minecraft_1.21.1_client.jar. Per-context display entries replace each other rather than merge, so overriding only the scale would silently drop the inherited rotation and translation; every context is declared explicitly.",
